{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3QaGkjzBEsyty4UEUYX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XwsnKLcrEQdfRnbXXk65ho","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"newlines. Every other byte is unchanged. TS in, TS out.\",\"newlines. Every other byte is unchanged, apart from the support import\\nbelow. TS in, TS out.\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/adr/ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"\n[adr-005]:\"\"\",\"\"\"\n## Note (2026-10-14): transform and final measurements\n\nTicket 14 made the `microtags/build` transform append\n`import 'microtags/render-support'` to any module where it keeps a\nrender link, unless the module already imports it. It is appended after\nthe last line so no existing line moves. A module where every link was\nstripped gets no import, with or without `cascade`. The plugins suite\nbundles two fixtures with the esbuild plugin and checks the metafile:\nthe all-stripped fixture has no support module input, and the\nkept-render fixture has one.\n\nFinal sizes in kB, brotli, measured with `size-limit` as above:\n\n| Bundle | Size |\n|---|---|\n| core (`index.min.js`) | 3.96 |\n| `microtags/htm` (server) | 1.93 |\n| `microtags/htm` (browser) | 5.29 |\n| example client, stripping on | 8.52 |\n| example client, stripping off | 8.64 |\n| all-stripped fixture | 3.63 |\n| all-stripped fixture, no plugin | 3.65 |\n| kept-render fixture | 3.95 |\n\nThe fixtures are `test/fixtures/support-stripped.ts` and\n`support-kept.ts`, bundled with `--minify` against source. The\nall-stripped fixture contains no support code even without the plugin,\nbecause core never imports it; the plugin only removes the render body.\nThe kept-render fixture adds the support module, about 0.3 kB. As\nexpected, the example's client still carries the support module through\nthe browser templater and Badge and Notice, so stripping saves only\n0.12 kB there (Counter's render body).\n\n[adr-005]:\"\"\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":680,"cache_read_input_tokens":104112,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":680},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15bf819d-2d04-4381-8228-4d11480b9c68","uuid":"04af9ef0-45b2-4d3f-a991-3da2019aa835","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:40:21.687Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3QaGVcdKYD89M1JMd4n","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XwsnKLcrEQdfRnbXXk65ho":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-14-transform-injects-support-import && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"newlines. Every other byte is unchanged. TS in, TS out.\",\"newlines. Every other byte is unchanged, apart from the support import\\nbelow. TS in, TS out.\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/adr/ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"\n[adr-005]:\"\"\",\"\"\"\n## Note (2026-10-14): transform and final measurements\n\nTicket 14 made the `microtags/build` transform append\n`import 'microtags/render-support'` to any module where it keeps a\nrender link, unless the module already imports it. It is appended after\nthe last line so no existing line moves. A module where every link was\nstripped gets no import, with or without `cascade`. The plugins suite\nbundles two fixtures with the esbuild plugin and checks the metafile:\nthe all-stripped fixture has no support module input, and the\nkept-render fixture has one.\n\nFinal sizes in kB, brotli, measured with `size-limit` as above:\n\n| Bundle | Size |\n|---|---|\n| core (`index.min.js`) | 3.96 |\n| `microtags/htm` (server) | 1.93 |\n| `microtags/htm` (browser) | 5.29 |\n| example client, stripping on | 8.52 |\n| example client, stripping off | 8.64 |\n| all-stripped fixture | 3.63 |\n| all-stripped fixture, no plugin | 3.65 |\n| kept-render fixture | 3.95 |\n\nThe fixtures are `test/fixtures/support-stripped.ts` and\n`support-kept.ts`, bundled with `--minify` against source. The\nall-stripped fixture contains no support code even without the plugin,\nbecause core never imports it; the plugin only removes the render body.\nThe kept-render fixture adds the support module, about 0.3 kB. As\nexpected, the example's client still carries the support module through\nthe browser templater and Badge and Notice, so stripping saves only\n0.12 kB there (Counter's render body).\n\n[adr-005]:\"\"\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01XwsnKLcrEQdfRnbXXk65ho":{"cwd":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-14-transform-injects-support-import"}}}
