{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3QdfQMCPGGQQdkuqMaY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012SLfXY85zjMcmCdVE1jKwD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rm -rf example-hydration/build test-results playwright-report && mkdir -p .nightralph && cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 14 notes: transform injects the render support import\n\n## Implemented\n- `src/build.ts`: `transform` sets `keptLink` when a define-chain render\n  link is kept (client:true or keep list). After strip and cascade it\n  appends `\\nimport 'microtags/render-support'\\n` unless the original\n  source already imports that specifier. Appending (not prepending)\n  keeps every existing line and column unchanged; imports are hoisted.\n- `example-hydration/vite.config.ts`: alias `microtags/render-support`\n  to `src/render-support.ts`, matching the `microtags` alias (otherwise\n  it resolves to `dist/` via package exports).\n- esbuild/vite plugins needed no change.\n- Docs: README (`microtags/build` \"Support import\" paragraph, render-support\n  section), ADR-009 note with final measurements, AGENTS.md learnings.\n\n## Tests\n- test/build.ts: kept link -> exactly one import, idempotent on re-run;\n  keep-by-tag; cascade keeps it and stays idempotent; no existing line\n  shifts; all stripped -> none (with and without cascade); no define ->\n  none. Red (5 fails) before the change, green after.\n- test/plugins.ts + fixtures `support-stripped.ts`, `support-kept.ts`:\n  esbuild bundle with an onResolve plugin mapping microtags to src,\n  metafile inputs checked for `render-support.ts`. Verified the kept\n  test fails against the pre-change build.ts.\n- Item 4 (example renders Badge/Notice after production build): covered\n  by existing e2e tests \"notice opens, dismisses, and opens again\" and\n  \"list adopts, adds, and removes keyed badges\"; no new test. Note that\n  the browser templater also registers support, so these do not isolate\n  the injected import; the metafile test does.\n\n## Measurements (size-limit brotli, kB)\ncore 3.96, htm server 1.93, htm browser 5.29, example client strip on\n8.52 / off 8.64, all-stripped fixture 3.63 (3.65 with no plugin), kept\nfixture 3.95. Measured with a throwaway temp dir (repo package.json +\nnode_modules symlink + temp .size-limit.js); removed after.\n\n## Gotchas\n- `dist/esbuild.js` (ESM) cannot be imported by plain Node ESM: it\n  fails `require('typescript')`. Use `dist/esbuild.cjs` from scripts.\n  Pre-existing, not fixed (out of scope).\n- First fixtures commit had a typecheck error (RenderContext uses\n  `props.count`, not `count`); fixed in a follow-up commit.\n\n## Gate\n`npm run gate` exit 0 (npm test 434, ssr 114, build 48, plugins 16,\ncli 23, hydration 136+17, hydration-dev 17, size ok). `test:e2e` 15/15.\nEOF\ngit status --short; git log --oneline -6"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":241,"cache_read_input_tokens":107649,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":241},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15bf819d-2d04-4381-8228-4d11480b9c68","uuid":"b080753d-dc69-48f4-a76a-1141d9f78435","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:41:11.379Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3Qdf8yCEM3NqHdibnea","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012SLfXY85zjMcmCdVE1jKwD":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-14-transform-injects-support-import && rm -rf example-hydration/build test-results playwright-report && mkdir -p .nightralph && cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 14 notes: transform injects the render support import\n\n## Implemented\n- `src/build.ts`: `transform` sets `keptLink` when a define-chain render\n  link is kept (client:true or keep list). After strip and cascade it\n  appends `\\nimport 'microtags/render-support'\\n` unless the original\n  source already imports that specifier. Appending (not prepending)\n  keeps every existing line and column unchanged; imports are hoisted.\n- `example-hydration/vite.config.ts`: alias `microtags/render-support`\n  to `src/render-support.ts`, matching the `microtags` alias (otherwise\n  it resolves to `dist/` via package exports).\n- esbuild/vite plugins needed no change.\n- Docs: README (`microtags/build` \"Support import\" paragraph, render-support\n  section), ADR-009 note with final measurements, AGENTS.md learnings.\n\n## Tests\n- test/build.ts: kept link -> exactly one import, idempotent on re-run;\n  keep-by-tag; cascade keeps it and stays idempotent; no existing line\n  shifts; all stripped -> none (with and without cascade); no define ->\n  none. Red (5 fails) before the change, green after.\n- test/plugins.ts + fixtures `support-stripped.ts`, `support-kept.ts`:\n  esbuild bundle with an onResolve plugin mapping microtags to src,\n  metafile inputs checked for `render-support.ts`. Verified the kept\n  test fails against the pre-change build.ts.\n- Item 4 (example renders Badge/Notice after production build): covered\n  by existing e2e tests \"notice opens, dismisses, and opens again\" and\n  \"list adopts, adds, and removes keyed badges\"; no new test. Note that\n  the browser templater also registers support, so these do not isolate\n  the injected import; the metafile test does.\n\n## Measurements (size-limit brotli, kB)\ncore 3.96, htm server 1.93, htm browser 5.29, example client strip on\n8.52 / off 8.64, all-stripped fixture 3.63 (3.65 with no plugin), kept\nfixture 3.95. Measured with a throwaway temp dir (repo package.json +\nnode_modules symlink + temp .size-limit.js); removed after.\n\n## Gotchas\n- `dist/esbuild.js` (ESM) cannot be imported by plain Node ESM: it\n  fails `require('typescript')`. Use `dist/esbuild.cjs` from scripts.\n  Pre-existing, not fixed (out of scope).\n- First fixtures commit had a typecheck error (RenderContext uses\n  `props.count`, not `count`); fixed in a follow-up commit.\n\n## Gate\n`npm run gate` exit 0 (npm test 434, ssr 114, build 48, plugins 16,\ncli 23, hydration 136+17, hydration-dev 17, size ok). `test:e2e` 15/15.\nEOF\ngit status --short; git log --oneline -6"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_012SLfXY85zjMcmCdVE1jKwD":{"cwd":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.hydration-dx-fixes-14-transform-injects-support-import"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012SLfXY85zjMcmCdVE1jKwD","type":"tool_result","content":"795e866 docs: support import injection and final ADR-009 measurements\nb785957 example: alias the injected render support import to source\n7841b5f test: fix support fixture render context types\n77f021e test: metafile shows render support only for kept render links\ne8883f7 build: inject render support import when a render link is kept\n9837beb nightralph: update ticket checklists","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15bf819d-2d04-4381-8228-4d11480b9c68","uuid":"4e9f35b4-f773-46f4-9255-693c77ca4333","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:41:11.528Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"795e866 docs: support import injection and final ADR-009 measurements\nb785957 example: alias the injected render support import to source\n7841b5f test: fix support fixture render context types\n77f021e test: metafile shows render support only for kept render links\ne8883f7 build: inject render support import when a render link is kept\n9837beb nightralph: update ticket checklists","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012SLfXY85zjMcmCdVE1jKwD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
