import it. Putting it last means no existing line moves, and imports are hoisted, so where it sits doesn't matter. A module where every render link was stripped gets no import, with or without cascade. The esbuild and Vite plugins needed no change.\n- **Example config:** `example-hydration/vite.config.ts` now points `microtags/render-support` at source, the same way it already points `microtags` there. Without that, the injected import would load from `dist/`.\n\n**Tests:**\n- **`test/build.ts`:** six new tests. A kept render link gets exactly one import, and running the transform again doesn't add a second (also with cascade). Keeping by tag name works. Original lines are unchanged. Fully stripped modules get no import, with or without cascade. A module with no `define` gets nothing. Five of them failed before the change.\n- **`test/plugins.ts`:** two new fixtures, `support-stripped.ts` and `support-kept.ts`, are bundled with the esbuild plugin, and the test checks the bundler's metafile. The support module is absent for the stripped fixture and present for the kept one. I confirmed the kept test fails against the old `build.ts`.\n- **Example renders Badge and Notice:** no new test here. Two existing e2e tests already create Notice and Badge in the browser from the production build. They can't prove the injected import is doing the work, because the browser templater registers the support module on its own; the metafile test is what isolates the injection.\n\n**Final sizes (kB, brotli, size-limit), recorded in ADR-009:**\n\n| Bundle | Size |\n|---|---|\n| core | 3.96 |\n| `microtags/htm` (server) | 1.93 |\n| `microtags/htm` (browser) | 5.29 |\n| example client, stripping on | 8.52 |\n| example client, stripping off | 8.64 |\n| all-stripped fixture | 3.63 |\n| all-stripped fixture, no plugin | 3.65 |\n| kept-render fixture | 3.95 |\n\nThe all-stripped fixture contains none of the server render code even without the plugin, because core never imports the support module. The example only saves 0.12 kB from stripping, because Badge, Notice and the browser templater still bring the support module in. ADR-009 already says to expect that.\n\n**Verification:** `npm run gate` passed (lint, build, typecheck, size and every test suite), and `npm run test:e2e` passed 15/15.\n\n**Also changed:**\n- **README:** documents the injected import and notes that a config aliasing `microtags` to source must alias `microtags/render-support` too.\n- **AGENTS.md:** notes that a script outside a bundler has to load `dist/esbuild.cjs`, because plain Node ESM can't load `typescript` from `dist/esbuild.js`. That problem already existed and I didn't fix it, since it's outside this ticket.\n- **Fixture fix:** one commit had a type error in the new fixtures that I missed at first. A follow-up commit fixes it.","ttft_ms":2919,"type":"result","duration_ms":304443,"uuid":"31347749-bc88-4834-bed0-3b2406903ff0","ttft_stream_ms":1564,"time_to_request_ms":59,"first_content_frame_ms":1564,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
